                        "entry_id": "82b91ece-0650-3926-8ec6-8c0c3358e0b1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A phenolic derivative of glycine, N-(4-hydroxyphenyl)glycine, used as a photographic developer."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "77cfd4d3-d6fa-4f94-a748-fc70f24f5ea5",
                                "sense_id": "88d7588b-6913-35d8-9b59-55930df11c19",
                                "text": "Glycin is a versatile paper developer that produces a strong, deep black on bromide papers and brown to sepia tones on warm-tone chloride and chlorobromide papers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a7b484e5-9761-4bfe-945d-469f144218ca",
                                "sense_id": "88d7588b-6913-35d8-9b59-55930df11c19",
                                "text": "Glycin immersed in LN₂ formed an amorphous product. Upon heating to –65 °C an unidentified crystalline phase of glycin was observed, which transformed at ≈ 55 °C to 2-glycin."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "51e344e6-f4ac-45c7-ac3c-a12bb3a4fafa",
                                "sense_id": "88d7588b-6913-35d8-9b59-55930df11c19",
                                "text": "Glycin developers are non-staining and have exceptionally good keeping properties, but are too slow in action for general use."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "774d601e-0756-321b-a131-d7233fa7d4b9",
                        "entry_id": "82b91ece-0650-3926-8ec6-8c0c3358e0b1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Misspelling of glycine."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
